# 19. API INTEGRATION

The backend is developed separately using Python Flask.

API base URL:

VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api/v1

Create a centralized Axios client.

Use the following API modules:

- authApi.js
- customerApi.js
- staffApi.js
- productApi.js
- planApi.js
- quotationApi.js
- subscriptionApi.js
- taxApi.js
- discountApi.js
- invoiceApi.js
- paymentApi.js
- billingApi.js
- dashboardApi.js
- reportApi.js
- portalApi.js

All frontend operations must call the corresponding backend endpoint.

Use:
- Authorization headers.
- Bearer tokens.
- Request interceptors.
- Response interceptors.
- Consistent error handling.
- Loading states.
- Pagination parameters.

Do not connect React directly to Supabase for business operations.

Authentication may use Supabase Auth client-side if coordinated with the backend authentication contract. All protected business operations must go through Flask.

If an API is not yet available, implement a clearly separated development fallback mode with sample data. Never mix sample data with production API results or silently pretend that a request succeeded.

